  "description": "VUCZOM crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 4 2 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C133 H132 Br16 Er4 O43 P8 2-,2(C4 H12 N1 1+). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 11 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 11 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 11 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 11 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 16 O neighbors; Er6 (Er) has 16 O neighbors; Er7 (Er) has 16 O neighbors; Er8 (Er) has 16 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.652-4.657 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 132.43-134.50°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Me4N]2[Er4(μ2-η1:η1-PO2R2)8(η2-CO2But)4(μ4-CO3)] (R = CH(OH)PhBr); anal. Br16C141Er4H156N2O43P8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
